A||N||3||sjp777||Ungodly slow power windows.||||1||
Z||000000||sjp777||04-04-2001||10:15 PM||||The power windows on my 88GT (Also on my previous 86SE) are irritatingly slow up and down. Is there a way to speed them up? I know they are like this from the factory. Most modern cars have much quicker up and down motion. Are there faster motors that can be retro-fitted? Also, the outer dew wipe on the drivers side is toast. It is scratching the window and the window rattles unless it is fully up or fully down. How hard is this to replace?||||reg||1
Z||000001||rogergarrison||04-04-2001||11:01 PM||||the dew wipes are apita. Lube is only thing you can do to the windows. what you got is what your gonna get.||||reg||1
Z||000002||theogre||04-05-2001||07:48 PM||||For a start pull the inner door skin. Then clean and grease the tracks. You want to grease the track on the glass and the vertical one that runs between the glass and arm rest mount.<P>Greasing the teeth on the big sector gear that the motor drive may also help.<P>Basically grease anything that moves except for the "felt" lined track in the front and back of the door.<P>I use "white" grease or lubriplate on them.<P>Dew wipes are a pain. but not rocket science.||||reg||1
Z||000003||FieroJoe||04-05-2001||10:24 PM||||Check this article out, it is the one I went by.<BR> <A HREF="http://members.nbci.com/_XMCM/fierov6/OSG/dew-wipes.html" TARGET=_blank>http://members.nbci.com/_XMCM/fierov6/OSG/dew-wipes.html</A> <P>A pain to do, and also helpful if you make your own tool (like the one rodney dickman sells, <A HREF="http://www.rodneydickman.com" TARGET=_blank>www.rodneydickman.com</A>  under tools section) or just buy his.<P>Greasing and lubing helped my driver's side window (pass. side is just fine!), but it is still slower and louded than the other.  Its just going to stay that way,  looks like too much of a hassle to replace the motor.<P>------------------<BR>AIM: Snowboarder0311<BR>87 Coupe 5sp. - big resto in progress<BR>  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/profile_1.JPG"> ||||reg||1
